General:
  UUID: "3de5fa6a-94cc-4936-9f31-c9ceee976100"
  Author: "sliptonic"
  License: "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  Name: "Northern Red Oak"
  Description: >-
    Northern Red Oak (Quercus rubra), clear straight-grained wood at 12%
    moisture content.
    Mechanical properties (specific gravity, modulus of elasticity, modulus
    of rupture, hardness, compression and shear strengths): USDA Forest
    Products Laboratory, Wood Handbook FPL-GTR-190 (2010), Chapter 5,
    Tables 5-1, 5-2, 5-3a. Public domain (US government publication).
    Density computed from specific gravity 0.63 at 12% MC.
    NOTE: Wood is highly anisotropic. The isotropic LinearElastic block
    below uses the longitudinal (along-grain) modulus E_L = 12.5 GPa.
    Transverse moduli are approximately 0.08 × E_L (tangential) and
    0.15 × E_L (radial). For FEM work requiring directional response,
    consult the FPL Wood Handbook elastic-ratio tables directly.
    Machinability data derived from FreeCAD core 'HardWood.FCMat'
    (Jonas Bähr, CC-BY-3.0, sourced from Zerspanung von Holz und
    Holzwerkstoffen ISBN 978-3-446-47769-8). The prototype targets hardwoods
    with density around 0.75 g/cm³ (beech, oak class); red oak at 0.63 SG
    fits within scope. Direction-of-cut significantly affects cutting force;
    values here are for the toughest direction (crosscut / Kivimaa A).
  SourceURL: "https://www.fpl.fs.usda.gov/documnts/fplgtr/fplgtr190/chapter_05.pdf"
  Tags:
    - "Wood"
    - "Hardwood"
    - "Oak"
    - "Red Oak"
    - "Quercus rubra"
    - "Northern Red Oak"
